From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] dsdmo: Implement the DirectSound effect DMOs.

The DirectSound effect DMOs (chorus, compressor, distortion, echo,
flanger, gargle, I3DL2 reverb, parametric EQ, waves reverb) were a shell
around IMediaObject. They now process audio: each object keeps its
parameters behind IMediaParams/IMediaParamInfo (ranges, defaults, curve
envelopes, GUID_TIME_REFERENCE), Set/GetAllParameters of the
IDirectSoundFX* interfaces check ranges, the I3DL2 reverb has its presets
and quality, and ProcessInput/ProcessOutput/Process run the effect over 8,
16 bit and float PCM in place. Parameter changes take effect without
clearing what is playing (delay lines, filter state); formats with an
inconsistent block alignment are refused. Removes ten todo_wine marks of
the dsdmo test.
